From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] radv: a PS4 winsys on Gnm

-Dradv-winsys=ps4 builds RADV for the PlayStation 4's Liverpool GPU
(GFX7, described as Bonaire) on the PS4 homebrew SDK
(src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps4):

- memory is libkernel direct memory, garlic (CPU write-combined) for VRAM
  and write-combined GTT, onion (CPU cached, GPU coherent) for the rest,
  mapped at one address for the CPU and the GPU; a window for 32-bit
  pointers is reserved within one 4 GiB block, 4 GiB where the kernel
  gives that much and 1 GiB or 256 MiB otherwise;
- command streams are copied into a garlic ring and submitted as DCBs
  with sceGnmSubmitCommandBuffers, followed by sceGnmSubmitDone; an
  EVENT_WRITE_EOP writes the submission's sequence number when it has
  run. Nothing runs as an INDIRECT_BUFFER, so the graphics preamble is
  emitted inline (RADV_DEBUG_NO_IB_CHAINING);
- radeon_info comes from the ac_fill_* helpers with Liverpool's
  configuration (18 CUs, 8 RBs, GB_ADDR_CONFIG and the tile mode tables,
  which match freegnm's and AddrLib's layouts);
- host pointers are imported where they are direct memory mapped for the
  GPU, as VideoOut's framebuffers are;
- the shader cache lives in /data/radv-shader-cache, in the database
  form, unless the title sets MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR or
  MESA_DISK_CACHE_DATABASE itself;
- RADV_PS4_PROBE submits one command buffer that only writes the
  completion marker, and RADV_PS4_TRACE tags each submission's progress,
  to tell a submission problem from a rendering one when the GPU hangs;
- a host build models the console with memfd mappings below 1 TiB, so
  device creation and pipeline compilation run on a PC.

There is no loader on the console, so the instance has no layers, and the
one GPU is enumerated without a device node. The conformance version
stays 0.0.0.0 until a CTS release passes.

